    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "a8582de3-dfc4-346e-b764-b2becf004bca",
                "word": "forehold",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e6a40e84-001f-4ca3-b822-b343ba293fb8",
                        "entry_id": "a8582de3-dfc4-346e-b764-b2becf004bca",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "foreholds"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7eba95cc-c0fe-3710-acbb-92c706138a5d",
                        "entry_id": "a8582de3-dfc4-346e-b764-b2becf004bca",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The forward or front part of the hold of a ship."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f9674b75-c434-4082-9b41-3b67719f3ac5",
                                "sense_id": "7eba95cc-c0fe-3710-acbb-92c706138a5d",
                                "text": "It freezes very hard, and we find it extreamly cold. The next Day, the ſame Weather, we went aboard, and ſcuttled for Flower in the Forehold. The 25th, little Wind at N.E. and froſty Weather, went aboard again, and got out of the Forehold eight Barrels of Flower, one Cask of Peaſe, with ſome Brandy and Wine."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0845fff7-ed9d-48ca-86ff-9d19ed6fb779",
                                "sense_id": "7eba95cc-c0fe-3710-acbb-92c706138a5d",
                                "text": "At nine in the evening, the Rippon, which ſtill remained aground, ran her larboard guns over the ſtarboard ſide, ſtarted thirty tun of water in the forehold, to lighten her forward, and employed all her boats in endeavouring to tow off: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6619a714-4b2d-4fdd-af61-6c5c2e92b682",
                                "sense_id": "7eba95cc-c0fe-3710-acbb-92c706138a5d",
                                "text": "Captain [John] Gore therefore ſent the carpenters of the Reſolution to aſſiſt our own in repairing her [the Discovery]; and accordingly, the forehold being cleared, to lighten her forward, they were ſet to work to rip the damaged ſheathing from the larboard bow."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c25f4147-66ac-4de6-af03-e7ded8d53da5",
                                "sense_id": "7eba95cc-c0fe-3710-acbb-92c706138a5d",
                                "text": "Extract of a Letter from an Officer belonging to the Major East-Indiaman, dated Calcutta, April 30 1784. […] The ſhip had been extremely infeſted with a kind of beetle called Cockroaches, which eat through every thing; and it was found neceſſary to fumigate the holds and decks, previous to her receiving the cargo on board, in order to deſtroy theſe vermin. In performing this buſineſs, by ſome accident, the fore hold of the ſhip caught fire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a7154de-3679-4d16-bbd6-279d55f54465",
                                "sense_id": "7eba95cc-c0fe-3710-acbb-92c706138a5d",
                                "text": "The salt provision rooms are on either side of the forehold amidships."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2b4ac8a-bb0f-40e1-ad39-2cdb73e8d657",
                                "sense_id": "7eba95cc-c0fe-3710-acbb-92c706138a5d",
                                "text": "I knew there was no other bulkhead in the ship but the collision bulkhead separating the forepeak from the forehold."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "21ce9115-05bc-49b6-938c-9741ecbe9ef1",
                                "sense_id": "7eba95cc-c0fe-3710-acbb-92c706138a5d",
                                "text": "If a total retarding force of 5,000 tons (which at least would be required by a 30,000 ton ship) is required, the aggregate area of the brakes must be 10,000 sq. ft., to accommodate which would very naturally reduce the capacity of the forehold."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0bf22d85-3c95-42c6-a2da-a97c791eb9fb",
                                "sense_id": "7eba95cc-c0fe-3710-acbb-92c706138a5d",
                                "text": "Quite a number of people recently gathered at the Wellington Wharf to watch the patent acetone process of cutting, with a flame forced out of a jet at terrific pressure, some steel beams and a bulkhead on a ship, the Arapawa, where it was desired to convert two foreholds into one."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c082498c-1829-4f6f-a4bf-5b7b431e4770",
                                "sense_id": "7eba95cc-c0fe-3710-acbb-92c706138a5d",
                                "text": "Everything about the steamers was filthy and neglected except the engines, which were in reasonably good order. The foreholds were crammed with ammunition, dhurra, wool and fuel, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "afb58bad-77f4-4540-859f-2cc3107a98d9",
                                "sense_id": "7eba95cc-c0fe-3710-acbb-92c706138a5d",
                                "text": "The forehold was a store for sails, warps and other gear and its floor covered a dank space known as the dill room where imperishable stores were stowed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6653031-fddb-4094-b6c0-c407d6256a2e",
                                "sense_id": "7eba95cc-c0fe-3710-acbb-92c706138a5d",
                                "text": "The third mate tried to retrieve the weapon from the two islanders who seized it, but when he saw a native approaching with a spear, he ran forward, barely escaping a spade thrown from the opposite side of the deck. He saw an open hatch and leapt for it, landing on the lower deck of the forehold."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
